<title>USA: Hurco settles patent issue with Siemens.</title>
<headline>Hurco settles patent issue with Siemens.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hurco Cos Inc said Thursday its IMS Technology unit settled a patent issue with Siemens AG regarding computer technology developed by Hurco.</p>
<p>Computer numerical control systems producer Hurco said it expects the settlement will increase net income by $250,000 in the fiscal year ending in October.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, IMS will license its patent to Siemens and certain related parties and Hurco will receive cash payments of $300,000 in fiscal 1997 and $750,000 in the form of discounts on future purchases of Siemens' products through December 31, 1999, Hurco said.</p>
<p>Hurco shares were up 3/8 at 5-3/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
